      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Using the fact that $-285^\\circ=30^\\circ-315^\\circ$, calculate the **exact** value of $\\sin\\left(-285^\\circ\\right)$ without a calculator.\n\n$\\sin\\left(-285^\\circ\\right)=$ {{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Write the angle as a sum or difference of special angles: $-285^\\circ=30^\\circ-315^\\circ$.\n\nRecall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(x-y)=\\sin x\\cos y-\\cos x\\sin y\n$$\n\nSubstitute the signed unit-circle values, multiply, and combine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sin\\left(-285^\\circ\\right) &=\\sin\\left(30^\\circ-315^\\circ\\right) \\\\ &=\\sin\\left(30^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(315^\\circ\\right)-\\cos\\left(30^\\circ\\right)\\sin\\left(315^\\circ\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}+\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4} \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
