      ":question/id": "a7f502c7-9d8c-5155-9c33-0ee994f82a79",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "What is the exact value of $\\sin\\left(-15^\\circ\\right)$ without using a calculator?\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $-15^\\circ=210^\\circ-225^\\circ$.*",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Write the angle as a sum or difference of special angles: $-15^\\circ=210^\\circ-225^\\circ$.\n\nRecall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(x-y)=\\sin x\\cos y-\\cos x\\sin y\n$$\n\nSubstitute the signed unit-circle values, multiply, and combine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sin\\left(-15^\\circ\\right) &=\\sin\\left(210^\\circ-225^\\circ\\right) \\\\ &=\\sin\\left(210^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(225^\\circ\\right)-\\cos\\left(210^\\circ\\right)\\sin\\left(225^\\circ\\right) \\\\ &=\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)-\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4} \\\\ &=\\frac{-\\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
