      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Using the fact that $255^\\circ=30^\\circ+225^\\circ$, calculate the **exact** value of $\\sin\\left(255^\\circ\\right)$ without a calculator.\n\n$\\sin\\left(255^\\circ\\right)=$ {{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Write the angle as a sum or difference of special angles: $255^\\circ=30^\\circ+225^\\circ$.\n\nRecall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(x+y)=\\sin x\\cos y+\\cos x\\sin y\n$$\n\nSubstitute the signed unit-circle values, multiply, and combine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sin\\left(255^\\circ\\right) &=\\sin\\left(30^\\circ+225^\\circ\\right) \\\\ &=\\sin\\left(30^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(225^\\circ\\right)+\\cos\\left(30^\\circ\\right)\\sin\\left(225^\\circ\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\ &=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4} \\\\ &=\\frac{-\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
