      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "What is the exact value of $\\sin\\left(165^\\circ\\right)$ without using a calculator?\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $165^\\circ=120^\\circ+45^\\circ$.*",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Write the angle as a sum or difference of special angles: $165^\\circ=120^\\circ+45^\\circ$.\n\nRecall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(x+y)=\\sin x\\cos y+\\cos x\\sin y\n$$\n\nSubstitute the signed unit-circle values, multiply, and combine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sin\\left(165^\\circ\\right) &=\\sin\\left(120^\\circ+45^\\circ\\right) \\\\ &=\\sin\\left(120^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(45^\\circ\\right)+\\cos\\left(120^\\circ\\right)\\sin\\left(45^\\circ\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
